{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe Reconciler Heartbeat Canary detected a persistent bridge outage. Three consecutive scheduled passes fail before config or network because the stdlib-only reconciler runtime imports optional `pydantic` at module scope. A separate preceding REB-3162 visibility failure remains tracked on `dutiable-shaded-honeyeater`.\n\n## Proven root cause\nCommit 557f8c16e35 introduced `runtime.py` with `from pydantic import SecretStr`; 40b8ac8295 eagerly loads that runtime from every pass. The bridge installs `.` with no extras, while `pyproject.toml` and `docs/config.md` require the engine/reconciler to remain stdlib-only and place Pydantic only in `[agents]`. Clean-venv, dependency-perturbation, and historical A/B runtime probes confirm this exact activation edge.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Replace the Pydantic SecretStr dependency in `runtime.py` with a frozen stdlib credential carrier. Preserve credential hiding from repr/equality/hash, exact reveal at adapter authentication, and accurate presence checks.\n- Strengthen the existing clean-runtime subprocess oracle in `tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py` to load the real reconciler runtime while Pydantic is explicitly unavailable.\n- Prove RED before repair, GREEN after a held-out fix, then RED again under the exact module-scope Pydantic mutation.\n- Sweep the reconciler engine for other module-scope optional imports and disposition every confirmed sibling.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py -q` for the clean-runtime subprocess oracle.\n- Run `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py -q` for credential and runtime behavior.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n- Build/install `.` in a fresh no-extras venv and import the packaged `rebar_reconciler.runtime` to replicate the original report.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py -q` executes the real reconciler runtime with Pydantic unavailable.\n- [ ] The clean-runtime subprocess imports no optional agents dependency.\n- [ ] Operation-binding tests prove credentials are absent from repr/equality/hash.\n- [ ] Operation-binding tests prove `reveal()` returns the exact credential.\n- [ ] The oracle is observed RED before repair.\n- [ ] The oracle is observed GREEN after repair.\n- [ ] Reintroducing the exact Pydantic import returns the oracle to RED.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] A fresh no-extras install imports the packaged reconciler runtime successfully.\n- [ ] The sibling sweep and dispositions are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787062945480862001,"uuid":"bb90a7f0-1b5d-4269-8963-e9885c14ccba"}